power: UMP9620 boards: one check for the board with a battery, before any register access

The F50 and the U30 Air share the UMP9620 device tree layout, charger, fuel gauge and USB-PD nodes included; only
the U30 Air has a battery, and only its tree has the stock charger policy service. One helper,
ump9620_has_battery_policy() in <linux/power/ump9620-battery.h>, answers for the bq256xx charger (0016), the fuel
gauge (0023) and the port controller (0020), and asks for the node to be enabled as well. The idea is kanoqwq's
(clean-tf-7.2, "battery board isolation"; mu300-linux f59a2968).

ZTE's charger node ("ti,bq2560x_chg") and the UMP9620's fuel gauge ("sprd,ump9620-fgu") end their probe with
-ENODEV on a board without it, before any register access. Under mainline the F50's gauge bound and listed a
"Battery" (sc27xx-fgu) with made-up readings: status Full, health "Over voltage", a temperature from an
unconnected NTC input, which every reader had to be told by the board to ignore; the charger read its node's
address before it gave up. Other SC27xx and BQ256xx boards keep their behaviour; the U30 Air is unchanged.

